# ── Claudette2 .gitignore ──
# Inverted model: ignore everything, whitelist framework.
# Child projects (their own git repos) are invisible by default.

# ── ⚠ NOT A MODEL FOR CHILD PROJECTS ──
# The inverted shape below — ignore everything, then whitelist the framework —
# is specific to what claudette IS. Claudette is a framework whose working tree
# contains other projects, most of them their own git repos; the default has to
# be "invisible" so a child's contents never leak into this repo, and the
# whitelist enumerates the framework itself.
#
# A child project is the opposite kind of thing: insular, owning its whole tree,
# with nothing nested inside it that belongs to someone else. It uses an
# ordinary deny-list — see .templates/child/.gitignore, which is the model.
#
# Copying this file's structure into a child would ignore that child's own
# source by default and track only whatever someone remembered to whitelist.
# Do not treat "how claudette does it" as house style.

# Ignore everything
*

# ── Root-level framework files ──
!/*.py
!/*.md
!/*.ps1
!/.gitignore
!/cboot

# ── Framework directories (fully tracked) ──
!/.codex/
!/.codex/**
!/.templates/
!/.templates/**

# ── State directory (structure only, see .state/.gitignore) ──
!/.state/
!/.state/**

# ── Testing group (shipped with platform, git-tracked) ──
!/Testing/
!/Testing/**

# ── Transient scratch (track only the charter, ignore contents) ──
!/.tmp/
!/.tmp/start.md

# ── Generated (never track) ──
.claude/
**/prefs-resolved.json

# ── Underscore-prefixed (invisible by convention, never track) ──
_*/
_*

# ── OS / editor artifacts (belt-and-suspenders) ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Secrets (never track) ──
.env*
*.key
*.pem

# ── Scrub output (pre-push artifact; reports embed matched lines verbatim) ──
# Must follow the whitelist block above: last matching pattern wins, and
# !/Testing/** and !/.templates/** would otherwise re-include these.
**/.state/tests/explicit/scrub/
